      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_29",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("As he enters the tunnel underneath Lady Karae’s manor, Darken Volk gestures, causing the entrance to collapse. The two necromancers turn and begin walking down the pitch-black tunnel, temporarily safe from pursuit."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_30",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Silence permeates the darkness, broken only by the irregular dripping of water from the musty cave walls. Malin looks toward Darken Volk occasionally, expecting something from the elder necromancer, but is met with stone-cold dispassion. There is no acknowledgment... no word of gratitude — only a sense of unease that has as much to do with the book as it does with Darken Volk."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_31",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("They continue walking through the damp, cold air all through the morning and day, finally emerging as the last rays of sunlight sink below the horizon."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_32",
